course: dictionary
lesson: 4683
title: Homeless and the homeless
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Homeless is an adjective, a describing word. Someone who is homeless has no home. They may sleep outside, in a shelter, or on a friend's sofa. «Kindness to people who are struggling, like buying a sandwich for a homeless man, treats people with dignity.» Here homeless tells you the man has no home.
explain: Add the word "the" and homeless becomes a noun for a whole group. «The homeless» means all the people who have no home. Check it by swapping your meaning into the sentence: "Help all the people who have no home" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Official words mean the same idea. "Rough sleeper" (official UK) means a homeless person who sleeps outside. "Person experiencing homelessness" (official US) also means a homeless person. These words describe a person's situation, not the whole person.
fact: Homeless means having no home.
fact: «The homeless» means all the people who have no home.
fact: People can become homeless after losing a job, becoming ill, or having family trouble or a disaster.
fact: Homeless people are people like anyone else, and they deserve kindness and respect.
fact: Charities, food banks and homeless shelters help people who have no home.
exercise: «Kindness to people who are struggling, like buying a sandwich for a homeless man, treats people with dignity.» What does homeless mean here? | *Having no home | Wearing old clothes | Very hungry | Happy and kind
exercise: Which words mean all the people who have no home? | *The homeless | Become homeless | Homeless kittens | A homeless shelter
exercise: Which official term means a homeless person who sleeps outside? | Night owl | Homeward bound | *Rough sleeper | Street dancer
test: Lily's dad lost his job and the family had to leave their flat. Her teacher says they have been "left homeless". What does this mean? | They have moved to a bigger house | *They have no home | They are going on holiday | They have won a prize
test: The charity runs a shelter that helps the homeless. Which group does this mean? | All the people who love cooking | All the teachers at the school | All the people who live near the sea | *All the people who have no home
exam: Which phrase uses homeless as a noun for a group? | Homeless kittens and puppies | A homeless shelter | *Help the homeless | A homeless man
